      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just updated my A records for a client site but the new IP isnt showing up for me yet. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually work everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This delay is due to DNS propagation, which is the process where changes are updated across various DNS servers worldwide. Different recursive DNS servers around the globe update at different speeds. The maximum time this can take is called the TTL (Time To Live), but it often resolves much faster than that.",
