      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, the TTL directly explains this varying experience. When a record has a high TTL, your local ISP or network might cache the old IP address for a long time. When you switch networks, you are querying a different set of DNS servers that may not have cached the old data, leading to different results for different users.",
