      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While outright ignoring updates is rare, inconsistencies can also arise from caching at the CDN or web server level, independent of pure DNS. If your client uses a CDN, they might aggressively cache the old site version or IP until their own cache expires. Alternatively, network routing issues between ISPs can occasionally cause transient inconsistencies.",
